TITLE: Basic JADX Command-Line Usage Examples
DESCRIPTION: Provides common command-line examples for using JADX, demonstrating how to decompile a DEX file to an output directory, set different rename flags (none, valid, printable), and control the logging level for operations.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/README.md#_snippet_11

LANGUAGE: Shell
CODE:
```
jadx -d out classes.dex
jadx --rename-flags "none" classes.dex
jadx --rename-flags "valid, printable" classes.dex
jadx --log-level ERROR app.apk
jadx -Pdex-input.verify-checksum=no app.apk
```

----------------------------------------

TITLE: Jadx Command-Line Basic Usage
DESCRIPTION: Illustrates the fundamental syntax for running Jadx from the command line, specifying input files and optional commands/options.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/README.md#_snippet_6

LANGUAGE: Shell
CODE:
```
jadx[-gui] [command] [options] <input files> (.apk, .dex, .jar, .class, .smali, .zip, .aar, .arsc, .aab, .xapk, .apkm, .jadx.kts)
```

----------------------------------------

TITLE: Install JADX via Flathub
DESCRIPTION: Command to install the JADX decompiler as a Flatpak application from Flathub.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/README.md#_snippet_2

LANGUAGE: Bash
CODE:
```
flatpak install flathub com.github.skylot.jadx
```

