TITLE: Install JADX on Arch Linux
DESCRIPTION: Command to install the JADX decompiler on Arch Linux using the pacman package manager.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/README.md#_snippet_0

LANGUAGE: Bash
CODE:
```
sudo pacman -S jadx
```

----------------------------------------

TITLE: Build JADX from Source
DESCRIPTION: Instructions to clone the JADX repository and build the project using Gradle. This process requires JDK 11 or higher to be installed.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/README.md#_snippet_3

LANGUAGE: Bash
CODE:
```
git clone https://github.com/skylot/jadx.git
cd jadx
./gradlew dist
```

LANGUAGE: Batch
CODE:
```
git clone https://github.com/skylot/jadx.git
cd jadx
gradlew.bat dist
```

----------------------------------------

TITLE: JADX Environment Variables Configuration
DESCRIPTION: Details various environment variables that can be set to configure JADX behavior, including security settings for XML and ZIP files, maximum allowed entries in ZIPs, and custom directory paths for configuration, cache, and temporary files.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/README.md#_snippet_10

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
JADX_DISABLE_XML_SECURITY: set to 'true' to disable all security checks for XML files
JADX_DISABLE_ZIP_SECURITY: set to 'true' to disable all security checks for zip files
JADX_ZIP_MAX_ENTRIES_COUNT: maximum allowed number of entries in zip files (default: 100 000)
JADX_CONFIG_DIR: custom config directory, using system by default
JADX_CACHE_DIR: custom cache directory, using system by default
JADX_TMP_DIR: custom temp directory, using system by default
```

----------------------------------------

TITLE: Install Jadx Plugin from Local File
DESCRIPTION: Details the pattern and an example for installing a Jadx plugin from a local JAR file. It also mentions an alternative method of copying JARs to a specific 'plugins/dropins' folder for manual installation.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/jadx-plugins-tools/src/main/java/jadx/plugins/tools/resolvers/README.md#_snippet_1

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
file:<path to file>.jar
```

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
file:/home/user/plugin.jar
```

----------------------------------------

TITLE: Install Jadx Plugin from GitHub Release Artifact
DESCRIPTION: Describes the pattern and examples for installing a Jadx plugin directly from a GitHub release artifact. It specifies the format including owner, repository, optional version, and artifact name prefix, along with how the artifact name is constructed.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/jadx-plugins-tools/src/main/java/jadx/plugins/tools/resolvers/README.md#_snippet_0

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
github:<owner>:<repo>[:<version>][:<artifact name prefix>]
```

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
github:skylot:jadx
github:skylot:jadx:sample-plugin
github:skylot:jadx:0.1.0
```

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
<artifact name prefix>[-<release-version-name>].jar
```

