TITLE: Jadx Core Command-Line Options
DESCRIPTION: A detailed list of core command-line arguments to control Jadx's decompilation process, output formatting, renaming strategies, and logging levels.

SOURCE: https://github.com/skylot/jadx/blob/master/README.md#_snippet_8

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
--deobf-res-name-source:
 description: Better name source for resources
 values:
 - 'auto' (default): Automatically select best name
 - 'resources': Use resources names
 - 'code': Use R class fields names
--use-source-name-as-class-name-alias:
 description: Use source name as class name alias
 values:
 - 'always': Always use source name if available
 - 'if-better': Use source name if it seems better
 - 'never': Never use source name
--source-name-repeat-limit:
 description: Allow using source name if it appears less than a limit number
 default: 10
--use-kotlin-methods-for-var-names:
 description: Use Kotlin intrinsic methods to rename variables
 values:
 - 'disable'
 - 'apply' (default)
 - 'apply-and-hide'
--rename-flags:
 description: Fix options (comma-separated list)
 values:
 - 'case': Fix case sensitivity issues
 - 'valid': Rename Java identifiers to make them valid
 - 'printable': Remove non-printable chars from identifiers
 - 'none': Disable all renames
 - 'all' (default): Enable all renames
--integer-format:
 description: How integers are displayed
 values:
 - 'auto' (default): Automatically select
 - 'decimal': Use decimal
 - 'hexadecimal': Use hexadecimal
--fs-case-sensitive:
 description: Treat filesystem as case sensitive
 default: false
--cfg:
 description: Save methods control flow graph to dot file
--raw-cfg:
 description: Save methods control flow graph (use raw instructions)
-f, --fallback:
 description: Set '--decompilation-mode' to 'fallback' (deprecated)
--use-dx:
 description: Use dx/d8 to convert Java bytecode
--comments-level:
 description: Set code comments level
 values:
 - 'error'
 - 'warn'
 - 'info' (default)
 - 'debug'
 - 'user-only'
 - 'none'
--log-level:
 description: Set log level
 values:
 - 'quiet'
 - 'progress' (default)
 - 'error'
 - 'warn'
 - 'info'
 - 'debug'
-v, --verbose:
 description: Verbose output (sets --log-level to DEBUG)
-q, --quiet:
 description: Turn off output (sets --log-level to QUIET)
--disable-plugins:
 description: Comma separated list of plugin IDs to disable
 default: (none)
--version:
 description: Print jadx version
-h, --help:
 description: Print this help
```

